APP("cradle_costs", "Cradle Costs", "Budget for the baby before the baby arrives", "Finance", ["#EC407A", "#29B6F6", "#FFCA28"], "baby",
 "Cradle Costs prices the first year of a baby, plans the income dip during parental leave month by month, works out whether going back to work pays after childcare, trims the buy-list to what newborns actually need, and lists the support to check for.",
 "You are a warm, numbers-first new-parent money planner: you separate marketing from need, plan the leave gap month by month, and never shame either parent's choice.",
 "Plan the year before it starts", "Due date, income and leave plans make the numbers real.", ["A first-year cost forecast", "Parental-leave cash plan, month by month", "Childcare vs going back to work, in numbers"],
 [NAME, TXT("due", "Due date / baby's age", "due 14 March"), NUM("income", "Household monthly take-home now", "4200"), TXT("country", "Country / region", "Ireland")],
 [T("buylist", "The buy list, trimmed", "Need, nice, skip", "🍼", [CH("budget", "Setup budget", ["Under 300", "300–800", "800–1500", "No fixed limit"], "300–800"), CH("space", "Home", ["Small flat", "House", "Sharing with family"], "Small flat"), TXT("have", "Already have / offered", "cot from sister, pram gifted")],
    "Build a newborn setup list for budget {budget}, home {space}, already have: {have}. Sections: table (Item | Need / Nice / Skip | New vs second-hand | Est. cost | Why); kv (total for needs, total with nice-to-haves, saving vs buying everything new); a callout on the few items to always buy new or check for recalls (car seat, mattress) plus safe-sleep basics; a checklist of what to ask family and friends for so you don't receive duplicates.", "table, kv, callout, checklist", "Trim the list", "Sorting the nursery…"),
  T("leave", "Parental-leave cash plan", "The income dip, month by month", "📉", [LONG("leave", "Leave plans and pay", "me: 6 months at 90% then 3 months statutory; partner: 2 weeks full pay"), NUM("costs", "Household monthly costs", "3300"), NUM("savings", "Savings now", "5000")],
    "Leave and pay: {leave}; household costs {costs}; savings {savings}; current income from the profile. Sections: table (Month | Income | Costs | Baby costs | Surplus / deficit | Savings balance) for 12 months from the due date; kv (lowest savings point and when, total size of the dip, monthly saving needed before the birth to stay above a one-month buffer); bullets on the least painful levers during leave (temporarily pausing pension contributions and what that costs, subscriptions, negotiating bills); a callout to get statutory entitlements and employer top-ups confirmed in writing before leave starts, noting rules differ by country.", "table, kv, bullets, callout", "Plan the dip", "Forecasting…"),
  T("childcare", "Back to work or not?", "Childcare vs salary, honestly", "🧮", [NUM("salary", "Returning parent's monthly take-home", "2400"), NUM("care", "Childcare cost per month", "1100"), CH("days", "Days per week", ["5", "4", "3", "2"], "5")],
    "Returning salary {salary}, childcare {care}, {days} days per week. Sections: table (Option | Net after childcare | Commute & work costs | Pension & progression effect | Net per month) comparing full return, reduced days, one parent at home, and a family-help hybrid; kv (break-even childcare cost, net gain per hour worked); a callout on the long-term cost of a career pause that never shows up in one month's maths, and on childcare subsidies or tax-free schemes to check locally; a quote with a message to a manager asking about a flexible or reduced-days return.", "table, kv, callout, quote", "Run the numbers", "Balancing…"),
  T("monthly", "First-year monthly budget", "What a baby costs each month", "📆", [CH("feeding", "Feeding", ["Breastfeeding", "Formula", "Mixed"], "Mixed"), CH("nappies", "Nappies", ["Disposable", "Cloth", "Mix"], "Disposable"), CH("stage", "Stage", ["0–3 months", "3–6 months", "6–12 months"], "0–3 months")],
    "Monthly baby budget for {stage}, feeding: {feeding}, nappies: {nappies}. Sections: table (Category | Low | Typical | High | Notes) covering feeding, nappies and wipes, clothes, health, childcare if any, transport, treats; kv (typical monthly total, cheapest realistic total, biggest swing item); bullets of 5 savings that do not compromise safety; a callout on growth-spurt and teething months when costs jump.", "table, kv, bullets, callout", "Show the budget", "Counting nappies…"),
  T("entitle", "What we're entitled to", "Benefits, leave and grants to check", "🗂️", [CH("work", "Work situation", ["Both employed", "One employed", "Self-employed", "Student / unemployed", "Mixed"], "Both employed")],
    "For a new-parent household with {work} in the profile's region, list the kinds of support to check. Sections: checklist of entitlements to look up (statutory parental pay and leave, child benefit or allowance, childcare subsidies, tax credits, one-off maternity grants, employer schemes, health-cost exemptions); table (Support type | Who usually qualifies | When to apply | Where to check); a callout that names differ by country, amounts change yearly and only official sources or an adviser confirm eligibility; steps for the first 6 weeks after the birth (registering the birth, adding the baby to insurance or health cover, benefit applications with typical deadlines).", "checklist, table, callout, steps", "Show the list", "Checking…")], FIN)

